  planner_response {
    response: "STARFALL\'s mouse flight control pipeline has been audited, decoupled, calibrated, and verified through live browser gameplay testing.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Final Calibrated Configuration\n\n| Parameter | Previous Value | Final Calibrated Value | Bounds |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| Aim Boundary Width | 40% | **40%** | 25% \342\200\223 70% |\n| Aim Boundary Height | 45% | **45%** | 25% \342\200\223 70% |\n| Boundary Shape | Rounded Rectangle (`r = 0.25`) | **Rounded Rectangle (`r = 0.25`)** | `0.05 \342\200\223 0.90` |\n| Precision Sensitivity | `1.00x` *(hardcoded + pre-scaled input)* | **0.50x** | `0.15x \342\200\223 1.50x` |\n| Boundary Sensitivity | `0.35x` | **0.30x** | `0.10x \342\200\223 1.00x` |\n| Maximum Sensitivity | `2.50x` | **1.80x** | `0.80x \342\200\223 3.00x` |\n| Acceleration Curve Exponent (`p`) | `2.0` | **2.0** | `1.0 \342\200\223 3.5` |\n| Angular Smoothing | *Implicit (~0.063s)* | **0.08 seconds** | `0.02s \342\200\223 0.25s` |\n| Reticle Recovery | `0.12s` | **0.12 seconds** | `0.04s \342\200\223 0.35s` |\n| Precision Inner Shaping Exponent | `1.15` | **1.25** | *(internal micro-aim curve)* |\n\nAll 9 calibrated defaults matched the target profile during browser testing and did not require overriding the initial values; raising the inner precision shaping exponent mildly from `1.15` to `1.25` further calmed micro-corrections (`15\342\200\22350 px`) without reducing full precision-boundary authority (`60.2 \302\260/s` yaw / `55.9 \302\260/s` pitch).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Pipeline Audit & Changes Made\n\n#### Root Causes Identified in the Mouse-to-Rotation Pipeline\n1. **Conflated / Duplicated Sensitivity Scaling (`FlightController`)**: `settings.mouseSensitivity` previously multiplied raw `mouseDeltaX / mouseDeltaY` *before* boundary clamping, while `evaluateProgressiveAxisSensitivity` ignored it and used hardcoded `normalSensitivity = 1.0`. Adjusting sensitivity therefore distorted both Aim Boundary reach and beyond-boundary excess accumulation.\n2. **Beyond-Boundary Bleed into the Precision Zone (`AimBoundary`)**: `boundaryBlendStart = 0.85` blended `boundarySensitivity` into the outer 15% of the precision zone (creating a non-monotonic turn-rate drop inside the boundary) and clamped `normalSensitivity` to `[0.5, 2.0]` and `boundarySensitivity <= normalSensitivity`.\n3. **Hardcoded Angular Response (`FlightController`)**: Ship angular smoothing was derived directly from `profile.angularDamping * 2.1` (~`0.063s` on Interceptor) with no independent `angularSmoothing` parameter.\n\n#### Systems & Files Updated\n- **Steering Configuration (`src/config/steering.ts`)**: Replaced `normalSensitivity` with `precisionSensitivity: 0.50`, updated `boundarySensitivity: 0.30`, `maxSensitivity: 1.80`, `angularSmoothingSec: 0.08`, `recoverySmoothingSec: 0.12`, `precisionExponent: 1.25`, removed `boundaryBlendStart`, and expanded independent `STEERING_BOUNDS`.\n- **Aim Boundary Evaluator (`src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`)**: Made `evaluateProgressiveAxisSensitivity` strictly return `precisionSensitivity` everywhere inside the rounded-rectangle boundary (`excessPx <= 1e-4`), with zero influence from `boundarySensitivity`, `maxSensitivity`, `accelerationDistance`, or `responseCurve`.\n- **Flight Simulation (`src/engine/FlightController.ts`)**:\n  - Removed the pre-boundary pixel multiplier so relative Pointer Lock deltas accumulate 1:1 into `virtualAimX / virtualAimY`.\n  - Wired `settings.precisionSensitivity` directly into per-axis progressive evaluation.\n  - Added independent frame-rate-independent angular velocity smoothing (`alpha = 1 - exp(-dt / effectiveAngularTau)` where Interceptor uses exact `0.08s`, scaled proportionally by hull inertia for heavier ships).\n  - Synced `reset()` and `centerAimCursor()` initialization with active `precisionSensitivity` (`src/App.tsx`).\n- **Settings, Persistence & UI (`src/types/game.ts`, `src/config/ships.ts`, `src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`)**:\n  - Replaced `mouseSensitivity` with `precisionSensitivity` and added `angularSmoothing` to `GameSettings`.\n  - Bumped storage migration to `starfall.settings.v5` so returning players receive the calibrated steering defaults while keeping graphics, audio, camera, and `invertY` preferences.\n  - Updated `SettingsPanel` and its live response curve preview to expose all independent controls (**Precision Sensitivity**, **Boundary Sensitivity**, **Maximum Sensitivity**, **Acceleration Distance**, **Response Curve**, **Aim Boundary**, **Angular Smoothing**, and **Reticle Recovery**).\n- **Preserved Systems**: `InputManager` Pointer Lock handling, relative `movementX`/`movementY` accumulation, continuous screen-edge turning, rounded-rectangle corner projection, camera controller, combat, AI, and mission systems were preserved unchanged.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Browser Gameplay Testing & Measured Results\n\nTested in headless Chromium (`1280\303\227720` viewport, Interceptor VX-9 Vanguard: `yawSpeed = 2.1 rad/s`, `pitchSpeed = 1.95 rad/s`) with `tsc --noEmit`, `vite build`, live Pointer Lock mouse dispatch through `InputManager -> FlightController -> GameScene -> FlightHUD`, and zero console or runtime errors.\n\n#### A. Measured Mouse Displacement vs. Ship Angular Velocity (Horizontal, `halfW = 256 px`)\n\n| Mouse Offset `dx` | Clamped Reticle | Outward Excess | Active Zone | Effective Sens | Measured Yaw Rate |\n|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|\n| `15 px` | `15.0 px` | `0.0 px` | `precision` | `0.500x` | **0.73 \302\260/s** (`0.013 rad/s`) |\n| `30 px` | `30.0 px` | `0.0 px` | `precision` | `0.500x` | **2.96 \302\260/s** (`0.052 rad/s`) |\n| `50 px` | `50.0 px` | `0.0 px` | `precision` | `0.500x` | **6.59 \302\260/s** (`0.115 rad/s`) |\n| `80 px` | `80.0 px` | `0.0 px` | `precision` | `0.500x` | **12.87 \302\260/s** (`0.225 rad/s`) |\n| `128 px` (50%) | `128.0 px` | `0.0 px` | `precision` | `0.500x` | **24.32 \302\260/s** (`0.424 rad/s`) |\n| `180 px` | `180.0 px` | `0.0 px` | `precision` | `0.500x` | **38.10 \302\260/s** (`0.665 rad/s`) |\n| `256 px` (Edge) | `256.0 px` | `0.0 px` | `precision` | `0.500x` | **60.16 \302\260/s** (`1.050 rad/s`) |\n| `286 px` | `256.0 px` | `30.0 px` | `transition` | `0.323x` | **38.89 \302\260/s** (`0.679 rad/s`) |\n| `350 px` | `256.0 px` | `94.0 px` | `transition` | `0.500x` | **60.10 \302\260/s** (`1.049 rad/s`) |\n| `496 px` | `256.0 px` | `240.0 px` | `acceleration` | `1.050x` | **126.29 \302\260/s** (`2.204 rad/s`) |\n| `736 px` | `256.0 px` | `480.0 px` | `acceleration` | `1.500x` | **180.40 \302\260/s** (`3.149 rad/s`) |\n| `1200 px` | `256.0 px` | `944.0 px` | `acceleration` | `1.709x` | **205.52 \302\260/s** (`3.587 rad/s`) |\n\n#### B. Vertical Precision & Acceleration Sweep (`halfH = 162 px`)\n- `15 px`: `1.82 \302\260/s` \302\267 `30 px`: `5.65 \302\260/s` \302\267 `50 px`: `11.75 \302\260/s` \302\267 `81 px` (50%): `22.58 \302\260/s` \302\267 `162 px` (edge): `55.86 \302\260/s`.\n- Beyond boundary: `+240 px` excess -> `117.27 \302\260/s` (`1.050x`); `+480 px` excess -> `167.52 \302\260/s` (`1.500x`).\n\n#### C. Continuous Swipe, Micro-Correction, Corner Clamping & Independence Verification\n- **Micro-Correction Tracking (`+25 px` for `0.30s`, then `-25 px` back to center)**: Peak yaw `2.11 \302\260/s`, total rotation `0.50\302\260`, stop overshoot drift `0.14\302\260`, residual yaw after `0.25s` = `0.093 \302\260/s` (predictable fine corrections with negligible overshoot).\n- **Continuous Outward Swipe (`0 -> 540 px` over `0.6s`, hold `0.2s`, return `0.4s`)**: Monotonic acceleration across all three zones (`6.6 -> 23.6 -> 45.3 -> 51.0 -> 63.1 -> 87.2 -> 111.5 -> 126.6 \302\260/s`) followed by clean recovery back into the precision zone (`91.1 -> 48.8 -> 16.2 \302\260/s`, `sensX` settling smoothly toward `0.500x`).\n- **Rounded-Rectangle Geometry & Corner Projection**: HUD verified `512.0 \303\227 324.0 px` (`40.0% \303\227 45.0%`), corner radius `40.5 px`. Diagonal `(420, 320)` projected smoothly onto the circular corner arc at `(244.6, 149.7)` with continuous turning (`93.26 \302\260/s` yaw, `80.94 \302\260/s` pitch).\n- **Time Constants (120 Hz measurement)**:\n  - Angular Smoothing (`0.08s` target): **0.0833s** to 63.2% step response.\n  - Reticle Recovery (`0.12s` target): **0.1250s** to 63.2% overdrive-to-precision recovery.\n- **Parameter Independence**:\n  - Varying `maxSensitivity` (`1.80 -> 3.00`), `boundarySensitivity` (`0.30 -> 0.15`), `responseCurve` (`2.0 -> 3.5`), and `accelerationDistance` (`240 -> 100`) produced **0.000 \302\260/s** change inside the precision zone at both `128 px` and `250 px` (near-edge).\n  - Varying `precisionSensitivity` (`0.25 -> 0.80`) produced **0.0 px** change in reticle clamping/boundary reach and **0.000x** change in Zone C beyond-boundary sensitivity (`1.050x` at `+240 px`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Remaining Issues & Recommended Next Phase\n- **Remaining Issues**: Automated browser verification used headless Chromium with simulated `document.pointerLockElement` for mouse delta dispatch; real-hardware human feel testing across varied mouse DPIs (800\342\200\2233200 DPI) is still recommended to confirm personal preference on `precisionSensitivity` (now directly tunable from `0.15x` to `1.50x` in Settings without disturbing any other parameter).\n- **Recommended Next Phase**: Playable ship unlock integration (Striker & Destroyer flight profiles verified against the calibrated steering envelope) or beginning the host-authoritative LAN/WebRTC multiplayer foundation once single-player flight feel is signed off."
